# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a preference.
#
# `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` is generated by `build/third-party-notices.mjs`,
# which writes `\n`, and `tests/manifest.test.ts` compares the committed file
# against a fresh render byte for byte. Git's Windows default
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites the working copy to CRLF on checkout, so on
# a Windows clone that comparison fails against a file nobody edited. Pinning
# `eol=lf` makes every checkout match what the generators write.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The pinned COPC slices are digest-checked by `tests/copc-fixtures.test.ts`.
# Git infers "binary" from NUL bytes today, which these have; saying so
# outright means the inference is never what stands between a fixture and a
# newline conversion that would silently break every digest.
*.bin -text
